A||||7||Adrift||Want to jack up rear of my fiero - Where to jack up / where to place jack stands?||||5||
Z||000000||Adrift||12-17-2001||09:39 PM||||I need to jack up the rear end of my fiero to pull off my wheels and change my brakes.. Where is the safest place to put the jackstands and where should I jack it up from ? (I have a 3000lb hydrolic jack and the jack that came with the fiero, as well as two 2000lb Jack stands).<P>If someone has PICTURES they can show me that would be best.<BR>Thanks<BR>Ari||||reg||5
Z||000001||Standard||12-17-2001||09:53 PM||||I always put the jack at the back of the engine cradle, in the middle.  The one right in front of the trunk.. Then I put jackstands under the right and left rails of the cradle.  Never had a problem.  If you need to jack it up really high you can put a 2x4 or something else to spread the load and jack from the bottom of the trunk, assuming it's not really rusted out or anything.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Adrift||12-18-2001||12:00 AM||||Any pictures? Anybody know how to do it "By the book"?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Neal||12-18-2001||12:08 AM||||I dont know if its by the book, but take a look under the car (assumption is pre 88) set the jack in the center, on cradle just infront of the e-brake equalizer.  Jack stands work perfectly at either side of the cradle, just behind the A-arms.<P>And always be sure to give the car a good shove when its all jacked up, just to make sure everything is secure and stable.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Adrift||12-18-2001||12:51 AM||||Got a picture of what the "A-arms" are?||||reg||1
Z||000005||REDHOTT88||12-18-2001||09:32 AM||||Adrift, don't freak out on the technical terms.<P>I just changed my oil by jacking up. If you look under the car, it will be pretty self explanatory.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>                                                                                                         <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/FIREdevil.gif">       <FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> <B>1988 Formula 2.8L</B> V6 5 speed </FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1">(Runs smooth, shifts crisp, red and shiny all over!)</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Archie||12-18-2001||10:05 AM||||Here is a Fiero engine cradle as viewed from the rear of the car. Notice (red arrow) the rear crossmember of the engine cradle kinda loop down. That's where you are going to place your floor jack.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/447.jpg"> <P>Here is an engine cradle in the car. Place the jack where I've put the red wire. Place your jack stands where I have the arrows.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/450.jpg"> <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Adrift||12-18-2001||12:16 PM||||Thanks Archie!<BR>Of course, my engine cradle looks nothing like that, its all rusted out! :P||||reg||1
